# Diff classification.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `packages/consent/src/adapters.ts` contains one NUL byte
# — the canonicalisation separator in `hashEvidence`, which is deliberate and
# documented at the call site. Git's binary heuristic looks for a NUL in the
# first 8000 bytes and finds it, so the whole file rendered as
# "Bin 10958 -> 13377 bytes" in every diff, every `--stat`, and every review.
#
# That is a real hazard here rather than a cosmetic one. This repository's rule
# is that safety logic must be readable in a diff — "a deleted prompt line looks
# like nothing in a diff" is why the prompt clauses have their own tests — and
# `adapters.ts` is the consent port: it decides which verification rails exist,
# which jurisdictions each serves, and how evidence is hashed. A silent diff on
# that file is exactly the failure the rule is written against.
#
# `diff` forces textual treatment regardless of content. It changes nothing
# about how the bytes are stored or checked out.
*.ts   diff
*.tsx  diff

# Genuine binaries, marked so no future glob drags them into textual diffs.
*.woff2 binary
